      "description": "This course aims at helping new students to develop an understanding and appreciation of university education and to adapt to campus life. Origins, traditions and objectives of universities, and their relationships with individual and society will be introduced. Distinctions between adult learning and juvenile learning, high-school and university studies will be elaborated. Advice and effective social and study skills will be provided to facilitate smooth transition. The Founder’s Ideas and the WS (Woo Sing) Spirit will also be covered.",
      "enrollment_requirement": "1. For Lee Woo Sing College Year 1 students only\n2. Not for students who have taken GEWS1012",
      "course_attributes": "Service Learning Course",
      "academic_career": "Undergraduate",
      "grading_basis": "Graded",
      "component": "Lecture\nProject\nInteractive Tutorial",
      "campus": "Main Campus",
      "academic_group": "Lee Woo Sing College",
      "academic_org": "Lee Woo Sing College",
      "learning_outcomes": "After completing the course, students will be able to:\n\n·Learn the Founder’s ideas and the WS (Woo Sing) spirit;\n\n·Understand the University’s origins, traditions and objectives;\n\n·Learn specific study and social skills; and\n\n·Raise their community awareness",
      "assessment_types": {
        "Essays": "30",
        "Presentation": "35",
        "Project": "35"
      }
