      ],
      "description": "A team is a group of two or more people who have a common objective or purpose with a commitment to collective and incremental improvement. Great teams, like great leaders, are made, not born. Two concepts, trust and commitment, are the glue that holds teams together. The objective of this course is to train the students to be a leader who can foster these two aspects of the team.\n\nIn this course, the students will learn the attributes of trust-building and commitment-building through lectures, workshops, and outdoor activities. The students will also participate in team projects designed by the College. By this chance, they will practise their knowledge and skills through thorough guidance by College supervisors.",
      "enrollment_requirement": "For Lee Wo Sing College students only.",
      "course_attributes": "Cantonese and English",
      "academic_career": "Undergraduate",
      "grading_basis": "Graded",
      "component": "Debate\nLecture\nProject\nInteractive Tutorial\nWorkshop",
      "campus": "Main Campus",
      "academic_group": "Lee Woo Sing College",
      "academic_org": "Lee Woo Sing College",
      "learning_outcomes": "• Explain the nature, purpose and structure of a team\n\n• Equip with the individual attributes that contribute to success of teamwork",
      "assessment_types": {
        "Essays": "20",
        "Lab reports": "25",
        "Others": "15",
        "Presentation": "40"
      }
