      "description": "This course helps students to understand the major concepts, theories, debates and reflections related to plant-based lifestyle. Particular thematic issues such as global warming and pollution, food crisis, diet and health, animal rights, social justice as well as green economy related to livestock industry and food system will be examined. The course encourages students to observe and evaluate the impacts of omnivore diet and lifestyle to their personal life, the animals and the planet as a whole.",
      "enrollment_requirement": "For Lee Woo Sing College students only.",
      "course_attributes": "Cantonese only\nService Learning Course",
      "academic_career": "Undergraduate",
      "grading_basis": "Graded",
      "component": "Field Studies/Field-trip\nLecture\nProject\nWorkshop",
      "campus": "Main Campus",
      "academic_group": "Lee Woo Sing College",
      "academic_org": "Lee Woo Sing College",
      "learning_outcomes": "By the end of the course, students should be able to\n\n• Examine the main concepts related to plant-based lifestyle, such as types of plant-based diet, development and consciousness in Hong Kong, modern livestock industry and global warming, correlation between diet and health in terms of nutrition, Chinese and Western medical science, animal rights of food animals and non-food animals and marketing direction of this movement",
      "assessment_types": {
        "Attendance": "5",
        "Essays": "40",
        "Presentation": "40",
        "Participation": "15"
      }
